WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:01.800
Good morning Hank, it's Tuesday!

00:00:01.800 --> 00:00:05.600
So several months ago, YouTube came to us to talk about a product they were working on

00:00:05.600 --> 00:00:08.180
I should stop here and say that in general, I dislike change

00:00:08.180 --> 00:00:11.620
Like I think YouTube reached its peak in July of 2007

00:00:11.620 --> 00:00:16.680
when our channel looked like this and the site went down for maintenance almost every single Wednesday

00:00:16.680 --> 00:00:21.360
I enjoy anachronisms like physical books, and I guess headphone jacks

00:00:21.360 --> 00:00:25.540
So I was a little dubious but I'm genuinely excited about this change, which debuts today

00:00:25.540 --> 00:00:28.940
But first let me back up and talk about a seemingly unrelated thing

00:00:28.940 --> 00:00:31.800
For the last couple years I've wanted to make a YouTube show about health and fitness

00:00:31.800 --> 00:00:32.960
called 100 Days

00:00:32.960 --> 00:00:35.460
where two ordinary people spend a hundred days

00:00:35.460 --> 00:00:37.420
eating well, exercising a lot

00:00:37.420 --> 00:00:40.600
and doing everything that's been proven by randomized, controlled trials

00:00:40.820 --> 00:00:42.080
to improve your health

00:00:42.080 --> 00:00:44.120
We'd work with experts to learn why it's so hard to make

00:00:44.120 --> 00:00:45.460
lasting changes in your life

00:00:45.460 --> 00:00:49.120
and along the way we would measure our progress by testing stuff we want to be better at.

00:00:49.320 --> 00:00:57.020
You know, like concentration tests, and push up contests, and hamstring flexibility, which at the moment for me, is just a little bit limited.

00:00:57.060 --> 00:00:58.680
But there were two problems with this show.

00:00:58.680 --> 00:01:05.640
First I didn't want to exercise and eat right for 100 days because sitting and pizza aren't just A way of life; they're MY way of life.

00:01:05.860 --> 00:01:12.740
And second we wanted to make this show with lots of infographics and pictures and recipes and live shows so it would feel deeply connected.

00:01:12.740 --> 00:01:17.520
But to do that would mean maintaining a billion new social media profiles.

00:01:17.800 --> 00:01:19.600
A thought I just could not stomach.

00:01:19.620 --> 00:01:25.640
This has been an ongoing problem because we've always had to built homes off YouTube for the non-video community stuff.

00:01:25.680 --> 00:01:30.460
Like if you want to submit a photo or a painting to the art assignment, you have to do so via Tumblr or Twitter or Facebook.

00:01:30.460 --> 00:01:33.460
we can't post worksheets or essays to accompany Crash Course videos

00:01:33.460 --> 00:01:37.260
and to full engage with the project for awesome you have to follow us on social media

00:01:37.260 --> 00:01:42.720
YouTube has always of itself as being about video, but for many of us its mostly been about community

00:01:42.720 --> 00:01:46.240
I'd argue that the best YouTube channels aren't just shows you lean back and watch

00:01:46.240 --> 00:01:51.380
They're communities you're part of and for a long time that was seen as YouTube's great weakness

00:01:51.380 --> 00:01:55.140
Like in the early days YouTube actually released a product called "Lean Back"

00:01:55.140 --> 00:01:59.640
that allowed you to watch videos without engaging with them because advertisers, espically back then

00:01:59.640 --> 00:02:04.820
thought that engaged viewers were bad news like for one thing engaged viewers are less likely to watch ads

00:02:04.820 --> 00:02:07.160
but also that the idea of mass media could be made

00:02:07.160 --> 00:02:11.380
and shaped directly by the masses was kind of terrifying

00:02:11.380 --> 00:02:14.200
but in spite of it all YouTube has continued to be a community platform

00:02:14.200 --> 00:02:18.360
and today they have embraced that with the release of the community tab

00:02:18.380 --> 00:02:23.600
this allows channels to post text, images, live videos and both jifs and gifs

00:02:23.600 --> 00:02:27.900
these will show up in your mobile subscription feeds and on desktop here in the community section

00:02:27.900 --> 00:02:30.020
you can also sign up to get new notifications for new posts in the community tab

00:02:30.020 --> 00:02:34.380
with say a book review or a live show or results from the Nerdfighter census

00:02:34.380 --> 00:02:38.120
its still in beta testing, there are lots of features to come but I am really excited about it because

00:02:38.120 --> 00:02:42.520
one it means that Hank and I can finally make our the community hubs we always wanted them to be

00:02:42.520 --> 00:02:46.580
two live shows are now easier and better, you can see this today when I do a live question Tuesday

00:02:46.580 --> 00:02:51.000
and three in our beta testing the quality of discourse in comments in the community tab has been great

00:02:51.000 --> 00:02:54.060
like upvotes actually work and also its much easier to moderate

00:02:54.060 --> 00:02:57.800
I just realized I'm being paid to say these things, to be clear, I'm not

00:02:57.800 --> 00:03:01.180
we have never and will never accept any kind of corporate sponsorship on Vlogbrothers

00:03:01.180 --> 00:03:04.280
but we did work closely with YouTube on the development of the community tab and

00:03:04.280 --> 00:03:08.040
I do think it's awesome which brings me back at last to 100 days

00:03:08.040 --> 00:03:11.700
so starting January 1st you'll be able to watch my best friend Chris and me

00:03:11.700 --> 00:03:14.500
try to have like the healthiest midlife crisis ever

00:03:14.500 --> 00:03:19.400
the show will not just include videos but exercise routines, recipes, live shows and text posts

00:03:19.400 --> 00:03:24.780
and it will all live right here on YouTube a community platform that also hosts videos

00:03:24.780 --> 00:03:29.260
Chris incidentally is known to Nerdfighteria primarily for once appearing in a Vlogbrothers video

00:03:29.260 --> 00:03:31.520
Wearing a speedo, but trust me you'll like him

00:03:31.520 --> 00:03:35.480
So you can head over to YouTube.com/100days and subscribe now if you want to see me preform

00:03:35.480 --> 00:03:42.280
like aerial acrobatics and hopefully, eventually, some day, touch if not my toes at least like my mid-shins

00:03:42.280 --> 00:03:45.460
in a live show later today I'll be answering your questions about 100 days and

00:03:45.460 --> 00:03:48.180
look forward to your ideas about how to make it awesome

00:03:48.180 --> 00:03:51.800
Hank, I will see you on Friday, actually I will probably see you before then

00:03:51.800 --> 00:03:52.760
thanks to the community tab

